a man accused of killing a teenage girl  during an apparent road rage attack in  Pennsylvania is in custody this morning  police arrested 28 year old David desper  yesterday he is charged with murdering  18 year old Bianca Roberson the recent  high school graduate died after she was  shot in the head on Wednesday DeMarco  Morgan is here with new details about  how the attack unfolded DeMarco good  morning good morning Jeff the Chester  County District Attorney says there is  no indication this is a hate or race  related crime desper didn't have a  serious criminal record and prior court  records reportedly show he drove an  unregistered vehicle and had inspection  violations  Bianca Robertson's parents sat in  silence on Sunday as authorities  announced the arrest of the man that  allegedly killed their daughter Bianca  Roberson 18 years old gunned down  because somebody didn't want to give way  somebody didn't want her to merge into a  lane of traffic david Esper turned  himself in to police early Sunday  morning he was arrested and charged with  first and third degree murder possession  of an instrument of crime and reckless  endangerment Tom Hogan it's the Chester  County District Attorney this appears to  be a savage senseless and brutal act  from one human being to another human  being according to police desperate  Robeson were attempting to merge into a  single lane of a suburban Philadelphia  Highway Wednesday afternoon as they  drove side-by-side jockeying for  position desperate pulled out a gun and  fired at Roberson striking her in the  left side of the head Roberson was  killed instantly her car crashing into a  tree along the highway desperate escape  was captured by surveillance cameras the  act of pulling a gun aiming the gun and  being able to shoot somebody in the head  from one moving vehicle to another is a  calculated act after a three day manhunt  investigators recovered espers of red  pickup truck and at despereaux's home a  40 caliber handgun suspected of being  used in the shooting according to court  documents  Destler had a permit to carry the gun  which he purchased in November 2015  Roberson was apparently on her way back  from  shopping when the incident occurred her  parents said she was preparing for her  first year at Jacksonville University  she was a good girl loved by many never  bothered anybody she was just a sweet  girl source close to desperate family  took CBS News they are devastated his  attorney declined to comment except to  say that desperate voluntarily  surrendered himself to police he's being  held in the Chester County prison  without bail Rena DeMarco thank you
 

